5. Citation Lookup Tool - CourtListener.com
   URL: https://www.courtlistener.com/c/
   Use our citation lookup tool to find case law by citation or to browse reporters. Our unique database of reporters and our extensive collection of citations makes for a powerful combination.

  librarian_tool_results: [{'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'prior art retrieval validation decision-making workflow precedent evidence', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'prior art retrieval validation decision-making workflow precedent evidence':\n\n1. PDF Topic 6: Retrieval and Comparison of Prior Art Citations\n   URL: https://www.wipo.int/edocs/mdocs/pct/en/wipo_pct_ge_22/wipo_pct_ge_22_t6.pdf\n   Need to be checked prior to grant decision If additional relevant prior art was found in other jurisdictions you need to consider it before granting Should be applied even when bilateral work-sharing agreements like PPH, Validation, Reinforced Cooperation or Parallel Patent Grant Initiative are in place\n\n2. Prior Art Search | USPTO\n   URL: https://www.uspto.gov/patents/initiatives/prior-art-search\n   One initiative of the Software Partnership is the investigation and sharing of search strategies, and the improvement of tools and resources to evolve better techniques to identify prior art.\n\n3. Innovating Patent Retrieval: A Comprehensive Review of ... - MDPI\n   URL: https://www.mdpi.com/2571-5577/7/5/91\n   Additionally, this dataset offers a well-annotated and standardized collection of patent documents, making the evaluation of prior art search and retrieval systems easier and more efficient.\n\n4. Optimizing Patent Prior Art Search: An Approach Using ... - ResearchGate\n   URL: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/389026531_Optimizing_Patent_Prior_Art_Search_An_Approach_Using_Patent_Abstract_and_Key_Terms\n   The refined prior art search promises to provide valuable assistance to specialists in their decision-making processes, offering insightful analyses and relevant information that can significantly ...\n\n5. H-ProtoRAG: A hierarchical prototype-based retrieval-augmented ...\n   URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306457326002529\n   To address these gaps, we propose H-ProtoRAG, a hierarchical prototype-based retrieval-augmented framework for joint CPC classification and prior-art retrieval in multilingual settings. At a high level, the model encodes the CPC hierarchy into a prototype-structured embedding space and couples this representation with a hybrid dense-sparse retrieval stack and a claim-evidence reader ...\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'feature request triage precedent corpus retrieval timing research phase', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'feature request triage precedent corpus retrieval timing research phase':\n\n1. Feature Requests: How to Collect, Triage and Close the Loop\n   URL: https://kompassify.com/blog/feature-requests-guide\n   A practical system for managing feature requests — where they come from and how each channel is biased, how to turn a request into a problem statement, a four-stage triage pipeline, how to decide, and how to close the loop when you ship and when you say no.\n\n2. Feature Request Analysis and Processing: Tasks, Techniques, and Trends\n   URL: https://arxiv.org/html/2508.12436v2\n   Goal — This research question aims to identify when the articles were published and how the number and frequency of studies have evolved; where feature request analysis and processing research has been published; what types of articles (academic or industry) exist; and how these studies address challenges related to feature requests.\n\n3. Feature Request Management: A Modern Framework for Product Teams (2026)\n   URL: https://www.koji.so/docs/feature-request-management\n   How product teams capture, triage, and prioritize feature requests at scale — RICE, Kano, and value-vs-effort frameworks, voting vs interview signal, and how AI-native research separates real demand from loud asks.\n\n4. Feature Request Analysis and Processing: Tasks, Techniques, and Trends\n   URL: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.12436\n   Feature requests are proposed by users to request new features or enhancements of existing features of software products, which represent users' wishes and demands. Satisfying users' demands can benefit the product from both competitiveness and user satisfaction. Feature requests have seen a rise in interest in the past few years and the amount of research has been growing. However, the ...\n\n5. Openclaw-examples/examples/runnable/25-feature-request-triage ... - GitHub\n   URL: https://github.com/McBorisson/Openclaw-examples/blob/main/examples/runnable/25-feature-request-triage/README.md\n   25 - Feature Request Triage Converts incoming feature requests into an evidence-ranked engineering queue.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'patent prior art search retrieval mechanism verification gate', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'patent prior art search retrieval mechanism verification gate':\n\n1. Google Patents\n   URL: https://patents.google.com/\n   Search and read the full text of patents from around the world with Google Patents, and find prior art in our index of non-patent literature.\n\n2. Prior Art Search | USPTOWIPO - Search International and National Patent CollectionsSearch for patents | USPTOEnd to End Neural Retrieval for Patent Prior Art SearchGoogle Patents Advanced SearchPrior Art Search: Complete Guide for Patentability, AI Tools ...\n   URL: https://www.uspto.gov/patents/initiatives/prior-art-search\n   See full list on uspto.gov See full list on uspto.gov For further information please contact us by e-mail or telephone: Contact: Seema Rao, Director, Technology Center 2100 (571)272-0800 See full list on uspto.gov 3 days ago · This patent search tool allows you not only to search the PCT database of about 2 million International Applications but also the worldwide patent collections. This search facility features: flexible search syntax; automatic word stemming and relevance ranking; as well as graphical results. Whether you’re starting your patent journey or are an experienced searcher, the following tools and learning resources will help you search for patents. Apr 10, 2022 · Off-the-self neural methods like BERT have lower effectiveness for patent prior art search. So, we adapt the BERT model to patent characteristics in order to increase retrieval performance. We propose a new gate-based document retrieval method and examine it in patent prior art search. Search and read the full text of patents from around the world with Google Patents, and find prior art in our index of non-patent literature. May 20, 2026 · Learn how prior art searches work, which AI tools to use, typical costs, best databases, and how to reduce patent risks before filing.\n\n3. WIPO - Search International and National Patent Collections\n   URL: https://patentscope.wipo.int/search/\n   3 days ago · This patent search tool allows you not only to search the PCT database of about 2 million International Applications but also the worldwide patent collections. This search facility features: flexible search syntax; automatic word stemming and relevance ranking; as well as graphical results.\n\n4. Search for patents | USPTO\n   URL: https://www.uspto.gov/patents/search\n   Whether you’re starting your patent journey or are an experienced searcher, the following tools and learning resources will help you search for patents.\n\n5. End to End Neural Retrieval for Patent Prior Art Search\n   URL: https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/978-3-030-99739-7_66\n   Apr 10, 2022 · Off-the-self neural methods like BERT have lower effectiveness for patent prior art search. So, we adapt the BERT model to patent characteristics in order to increase retrieval performance. We propose a new gate-based document retrieval method and examine it in patent prior art search.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'evidence retrieval timing decision workflow gate validation before conclusion', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'evidence retrieval timing decision workflow gate validation before conclusion':\n\n1. Evidence Flow + Execution Model - arxiu.io\n   URL: https://www.arxiu.io/docs/decision-gate/guides/evidence-flow-and-execution-model\n   Evidence Flow + Execution Model At a Glance What: How Decision Gate evaluates evidence and produces decisions Why: Understand exactly what is fetched, validated, and compared Who: Developers, security teams, and architects integrating Decision Gate Prerequisites: getting_started.md One Sentence You Must Remember Decision Gate evaluates evidence; it does not execute tasks.\n\n2. Verification Workflow: Evidence-First Principle, Gate Function Flow ...\n   URL: https://lzw.me/docs/opencodedocs/obra/superpowers/core-workflows/verification-workflow/\n   Learn verification skills and master the evidence-first principle. This tutorial covers the verification iron rule, the complete 5-step gate function workflow, 8 common failure cases, and red flags criteria. It ensures AI agents must provide authentic verification evidence before claiming completion, avoiding false success claims and rationalizations, ensuring code quality, build credibility ...\n\n3. PAVE: Premise-Grounded Answer Validation and Editing for Retrieval ...\n   URL: https://arxiv.org/html/2603.20673v2\n   Abstract Retrieval-augmented language models can retrieve relevant evidence yet still commit to answers before explicitly checking whether the retrieved context supports the conclusion. We present PAVE (Premise-Grounded Answer Validation and Editing), an inference-time validation layer for evidence-grounded question answering.\n\n4. Proactive Research Needs a Decision Gate - Fred\n   URL: https://meet-fred.com/resources/research-operations/proactive-research-decision-gates-ai-insight-pipelines\n   Govern proactive UX research with a decision gate that tests relevance, evidence gaps, source boundaries, ownership, and measurable decision impact.\n\n5. AIES Validation Evidence Package and Release Gates\n   URL: https://www.ai-standards.dev/docs/validation/evidence-and-release-gates\n   Define the immutable evidence package, review controls, publication boundary, and release decision required before AIES may claim external validation.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'deterministic context injection closed-input research boundary precedent corpus', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'deterministic context injection closed-input research boundary precedent corpus':\n\n1. GitHub - SpeeedPenguin/deterministic-context-architecture...\n   URL: https://github.com/SpeeedPenguin/deterministic-context-architecture-\n   Deterministic Context Architecture (DCA) is an input interface engineering framework designed to minimize variance in stochastic LLM outputs through spatial token constraints, attentional detuning, and stateless session lifecycle control. Overview / ...\n\n2. Goodbye AI Drift! The Deterministic Context Layer: Removing...\n   URL: https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/deterministic-context-layer-removing-ais-reliance-model-ryan-jordan-3skqe\n   Every piece of critical context — decisions, insights, strategic facts, behavioral rules, user preferences — is persisted externally from the model. Before every request, this context is assembled through a deterministic pipeline and injected into the prompt.\n\n3. Deterministic Enforcement — Mneme HQ Concepts\n   URL: https://mnemehq.com/concepts/deterministic-enforcement/\n   Deterministic enforcement. A governance check that produces the same verdict for the same code, the same decision corpus, and the same context — every time, independent of model state, retrieval variance, or runtime conditions. Determinism is not a performance property.\n\n4. Deterministic context-free language\n   URL: https://grokipedia.com/page/Deterministic_context-free_language\n   Deterministic context-free languages (DCFLs) exhibit several closure properties that distinguish them from the broader class of context-free languages (CFLs). Notably, DCFLs are closed under complementation, a property not shared by CFLs.\n\n5. Powering AI-ready modernization with AI + CAST and deterministic...\n   URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CJL_hWAV7hA\n   Shikhar Saran, Director Consulting Delivery at CGI, shares how CAST's deterministic architectural context brings clarity to brownfield systems and makes AI-driven modernization safe, accurate, and scalable. … ...ещё.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': '"retrieval-augmented generation" evidence validation corpus injection research phase', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': 'Search results for \'"retrieval-augmented generation" evidence validation corpus injection research phase\':\n\n1. RAG Isn’t Safer: 9 Injection Paths Through Retrieved Text | Medium\n   URL: https://medium.com/@Praxen/rag-isnt-safer-9-injection-paths-through-retrieved-text-41421c23ad8d\n   Why retrieval-augmented generation can reduce hallucinations yet still open new prompt injection paths teams routinely underestimate.A lot of teams treat retrieval-augmented generation like a security upgrade by default. The model is grounded now, they say.\n\n2. RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation) — простое... / Хабр\n   URL: https://habr.com/ru/articles/779526/\n   RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation) — это метод работы с большими языковыми моделями, когда пользователь пишет свой вопросы, а вы программно к этому вопросу «подмешиваете» дополнительную информацию из...\n\n3. Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Large Language Models...\n   URL: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2312.10997v1\n   Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) refers to the retrieval of relevant information from external knowledge bases before answering ques-tions with LLMs.In summary, the advantages and limitations of augmented pre-training are evident.\n\n4. Retrieval-Augmented Generation\n   URL: https://dejan.ai/concepts/retrieval-augmented-generation/\n   Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a framework that fetches relevant evidence before the model writes, then feeds the query plus that evidence into the model in a single context window.\n\n5. RAG explained without the hype. RAG = Retrieval-Augmented...\n   URL: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/neuronetis_rag-explained-without-the-hype-rag-retrieval-augmented-activity-7449952724411949056-lmCD\n   RAG = Retrieval-Augmented Generation. Instead of asking an LLM what it knows, you ask it to answer based on documents you provide.It is chunking, rewriting, reranking, and validation working together. That’s how modern RAG systems are built. Naive retrieval is only step one.\n', 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'RAG pipeline corpus context window precedent lookup before generation', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': 'Search results for \'RAG pipeline corpus context window precedent lookup before generation\':\n\n1. Mastering RAG Pipelines: A Comprehensive Guide to Retrieval-Augmented ...\n   URL: https://martinuke0.github.io/posts/2026-01-06-mastering-rag-pipelines-a-comprehensive-guide-to-retrieval-augmented-generation/\n   What is a RAG Pipeline? A RAG pipeline bridges LLMs with external knowledge bases, typically unstructured data from databases, documents, or data lakes, by retrieving relevant context before generation. [1] [8] It operates in two main phases: indexing (offline preparation of data) and retrieval-generation (online query processing). [1] [4]\n\n2. RAG and Context Injection: Pipeline Design Guide 2026 - explainx.ai\n   URL: https://www.explainx.ai/blog/rag-context-injection-pipeline-design-2026\n   Retrieval-augmented generation is a context engineering problem. This guide covers the full pipeline: chunking strategies, embedding models, retrieval scoring, context injection patterns, and the common failure modes that cause RAG systems to underperform in production.\n\n3. Understanding the Context Window in RAG and Agentic RAG\n   URL: https://medium.com/@dewasheesh.rana/by-dewasheesh-rana-b8404b0acb85\n   In Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), external documents are fetched and added to the LLM prompt. However, the context window limits how much retrieved text can fit.\n\n4. Contextual Retrieval in AI Systems \\ Anthropic\n   URL: https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/contextual-retrieval\n   A primer on RAG: scaling to larger knowledge bases For larger knowledge bases that don\'t fit within the context window, RAG is the typical solution. RAG works by preprocessing a knowledge base using the following steps: Break down the knowledge base (the "corpus" of documents) into smaller chunks of text, usually no more than a few hundred ...\n\n5. GitHub - HarinezumIgel/RAG-LCC: Experimental RAG playground for ...\n   URL: https://github.com/HarinezumIgel/RAG-LCC\n   RAG‑LCC (Retrieval‑Augmented Generation — Local Corpus & Classification) is an experimental lab for studying and addressing these failure modes. Instead of pushing ever‑larger context windows, it treats classification, chunking, retrieval strategy, and content filtering as first‑class architectural decisions.\n', 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'gate checks substance not shape evidence validation decision system', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'gate checks substance not shape evidence validation decision system':\n\n1. Field Level Validation for Document AI: A Practical Guide | Matil\n   URL: https://matil.ai/en/blog/field-level-validation\n   What Field Level Validation Means in a Document Pipeline. Field level validation evaluates one extracted value at a time. The system checks whether the value has the expected data type, follows the required pattern, fits an acceptable range, and exists when the field is mandatory.\n\n2. Gates Product Validation\n   URL: https://productvalidation.gates.com/\n   © 2026 Gates Corporation, All Rights Reserved.\n\n3. GATE 2027 | Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering (GATE)\n   URL: https://gate2027.iitm.ac.in/\n   The syllabi for the GATE 2027 test papers have been revised. Candidates are advised to check the updated syllabi. GATE 2027 Registration through DigiLocker is mandatory for all Indian nationals.\n\n4. 8.24.26 Daily Briefing: GEO Tricks...Demoted. Your Evidence, Earned...\n   URL: https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/82426-daily-briefing-geo-tricksdemoted-your-evidence-earned-authority-nmz2c\n   When AI systems summarize a perceived consensus before users inspect individual sources, credible third-party evidence and recognizable authority become part of the decision experience itself. Global consistency needs local interpretation checks.\n\n5. Evidence Based Medicine – New Approaches and Challenges - PMC\n   URL: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3789163/\n   CONFLICT OF INTEREST: NONE DECLARED Evidence based medicine (EBM) is the conscientious, explicit, judicious and reasonable use of modern, best evidence in making decisions about the care of individual patients.\n", 'success': True}, {'tool': 'search_web', 'args': {'query': 'precedent citation verification lookup mechanism before decision finalization', 'max_results': 5}, 'output': "Search results for 'precedent citation verification lookup mechanism before decision finalization':\n\n1. JurisCheck - Citation Verification for Legal Documents\n   URL: https://www.jurischeck.com/\n   JurisCheck is a Bluebook-native legal citation verification service that helps attorneys, legal teams, and scholars confirm authorities before filing briefs, memos, and journal articles.\n\n2. FinalVerify — Citation Verification for Legal Professionals\n   URL: https://finalverify.com/\n   Verify Every Citation Before You File FinalVerify checks your case citations, statutes, and references against authoritative databases — and shows you exactly how each one was verified.\n\n3. PrecedentPilot — Search\n   URL: https://precedentpilot.com/\n   PrecedentPilot: unified legal search across facts, rules, and case names — plus Amelia, your AI legal research assistant.\n\n4. Veridictum - Legal Citation Verification\n   URL: https://veridictum.legal/\n   Search 539,000+ precedential cases by legal topic or keyword Smart Case Ranking - landmark cases and highly-cited precedent appear first Citation lookup - enter a citation to find the case and related cases Search by legal topic across 539,000+ precedential cases Photo Quick Lookup - snap a citation, get instant results\n\n5. Citation Lookup Tool - CourtListener.com\n   URL: https://www.courtlistener.com/c/\n   Use our citation lookup tool to find case law by citation or to browse reporters. Our unique database of reporters and our extensive collection of citations makes for a powerful combination.\n", 'success': True}]
  librarian_finding: {'persona': 'librarian', 'candidate': 'Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines inject external corpus context deterministically before generation, separating retrieval timing from conclusion finalization. RAG operates in two phases: offline indexing and online retrieval-generation, ensuring evidence is fetched and validated before the model commits to answers.', 'solution_class': 'external-method', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'https://martinuke0.github.io/posts/2026-01-06-mastering-rag-pipelines-a-comprehensive-guide-to-retrieval-augmented-generation/', 'is_this_a_graph': "Yes. RAG pipelines are graph-structured workflows with indexing and retrieval-generation phases, matching the research route's fan-out topology and deterministic context injection pattern.", 'effort_risk': 'Medium. RAG requires corpus preprocessing and embedding infrastructure, but the pattern directly addresses the timing problem: retrieval happens before generation, not after conclusions freeze.', 'rationale': 'The brief identifies that prior-art retrieval fires after research conclusions are frozen, violating the doctrine that precedent must be known before authority is granted. RAG solves this by making retrieval a mandatory upstream phase before any generation step, ensuring evidence is available and validated before the decision agent commits.'}
  findings: [{'persona': 'os-infra-primitivist', 'candidate': 'Inject a deterministic, author-independent FR-corpus index into the committed-context block at research-graph startup. Index contains only FR filenames and their creation timestamps, built by a pre-research hook that reads `feature-requests/*.md` once and serializes the list as immutable context.', 'solution_class': 'boundary-enforcement', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-890 R-2 (closed input boundary); FR-896 (precedent traceability); CAP-248 (research sole route); gate_checks_shape_not_substance (Scripture)', 'is_this_a_graph': "No. The index is a static data artifact injected into the research graph's context block, not a graph mechanism itself.", 'effort_risk': 'Low/medium. Effort: add a pre-research hook to serialize FR filenames and timestamps into context. Risk: context size must stay under `_MAX_CONTEXT_LINES`; 854 files as one-liners fit easily.', 'rationale': 'The research personas already receive a deterministic context block from `collect_committed_context`. Adding an FR-corpus index there preserves closure (author-independent, committed, immutable) while giving personas a lookup table to ground precedent citations. This shifts precedent retrieval from persona memory to a verifiable artifact the personas can cite by filename.'}, {'persona': 'data-process-planner', 'candidate': 'Inject deterministic FR-corpus summary (854-file digest: count, recency, rejection-rate) into committed_context block before research runs, enabling personas to cite real precedent without author narrative.', 'solution_class': 'schema-data', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-890 R-2 (closed input boundary); gate_checks_shape_not_substance (Scripture); FR-737 F4 (witnessed miss escalation); CAP-248 (research sole route).', 'is_this_a_graph': 'No. This is a schema and lifecycle change: add a deterministic, author-independent corpus digest to the committed context block before research graph invocation.', 'effort_risk': 'Medium effort, low risk. Digest generation is deterministic and bounded (one-liner per FR: ID, status, date). Fits within _MAX_CONTEXT_LINES. No persona or artifact schema changes required.', 'rationale': 'Research runs blind to prior art because the FR corpus is not in committed_context. Injecting a digest (not full corpus) respects the closed-input boundary, gives personas a verifiable precedent anchor, and moves retrieval upstream—before conclusions freeze—without author narrative.'}, {'persona': 'yamlgraph-native-planner', 'candidate': 'Inject a deterministic prior-art corpus digest into committed_context via a new `_collect_prior_art` function. Rank FRs by filename-noun IDF, cap at 20 rows, and append as a read-only reference block alongside capability registry and ARCHITECTURE headings.', 'solution_class': 'schema-data', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-890 R-2 (closed-input boundary), FR-896 (research-route precedent traceability), gate_checks_shape_not_substance (Scripture)', 'is_this_a_graph': 'corpus-census: deterministic collection, extraction bound at invocation time, reducer owns output rendering.', 'effort_risk': 'Medium: extends committed_context block within _MAX_CONTEXT_LINES budget; reuses existing prior-art.py noun extraction and IDF ranking; no schema column changes required.', 'rationale': 'Moves precedent retrieval into the research phase by making prior-art results a deterministic, author-independent input. Personas cite from a corpus digest they can see, not from memory. Judge receives FR + research artifact + prior-art reference, closing the evidence chain.'}, {'persona': 'subtractionist', 'candidate': 'Delete the frozen `precedent` column shape check from `scripts/research_preflight.py` and `research_tools.py`. Personas already cannot access the FR corpus; requiring them to cite it is a gate that fails on its own constraint. Let the Judge receive raw research rows and validate precedent substance itself.', 'solution_class': 'schema-data', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'FR-890 R-2 (closed input boundary); gate_checks_shape_not_substance (Scripture); FR-737 F4 (witnessed escalation beyond filenames requires a miss).', 'is_this_a_graph': 'No. This is a schema and validation removal, not a graph dependency or retrieval problem.', 'effort_risk': "Low. Delete two validation blocks and one column constraint. Risk: research rows may carry empty or false precedent; Judge must then enforce substance. That is already the Judge's role.", 'rationale': 'The precedent column is currently shape-checked for non-emptiness only, yet 15 of 60 rows cite nothing verifiable. Personas have no access to the FR corpus, so the gate is a false boundary. Removing the shape check stops pretending the research step can validate what it cannot see, and moves substance validation to the Judge—where the FR, doctrine, and evidence are all present.'}, {'persona': 'librarian', 'candidate': 'Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines inject external corpus context deterministically before generation, separating retrieval timing from conclusion finalization. RAG operates in two phases: offline indexing and online retrieval-generation, ensuring evidence is fetched and validated before the model commits to answers.', 'solution_class': 'external-method', 'verdict': 'pursue', 'precedent': 'https://martinuke0.github.io/posts/2026-01-06-mastering-rag-pipelines-a-comprehensive-guide-to-retrieval-augmented-generation/', 'is_this_a_graph': "Yes. RAG pipelines are graph-structured workflows with indexing and retrieval-generation phases, matching the research route's fan-out topology and deterministic context injection pattern.", 'effort_risk': 'Medium. RAG requires corpus preprocessing and embedding infrastructure, but the pattern directly addresses the timing problem: retrieval happens before generation, not after conclusions freeze.', 'rationale': 'The brief identifies that prior-art retrieval fires after research conclusions are frozen, violating the doctrine that precedent must be known before authority is granted. RAG solves this by making retrieval a mandatory upstream phase before any generation step, ensuring evidence is available and validated before the decision agent commits.'}]
